  <entry>
    <id>tag:github.com,2008:Grit::Commit/b8150de8e78f933e515cc46c6fce44b9bc86a395</id>
    <link type="text/html" rel="alternate" href="https://github.com/nonkuri/obsidian-vivlio/commit/b8150de8e78f933e515cc46c6fce44b9bc86a395"/>
    <title>
        fix: typeset math instead of leaving LaTeX on the page
    </title>
    <updated>2026-09-12T09:00:04Z</updated>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/290948908?s=30&amp;v=4"/>
    <author>
      <name>nonkuri</name>
      <uri>https://github.com/nonkuri</uri>
    </author>
    <content type="html">
      &lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;fix: typeset math instead of leaving LaTeX on the page

VFM&amp;#39;s default math renderer keeps the LaTeX as text and loads MathJax from
a CDN to set it in the reader. sanitizePlugin takes that script back out -
a book does not run code - so every formula reached the page as bare
`\(x\)` source, which the notation rules then read as ordinary text. An
EPUB and a PDF have nowhere to run the script anyway, and a vault may have
no network. Force `mathRenderer: &amp;quot;mathml&amp;quot;`, so Temml converts the LaTeX
while the book is built, and warn when a book asks for another renderer.

The blank-line counter then had to learn that &amp;lt;math&amp;gt; is not a block read
off the manuscript: Temml&amp;#39;s fragment carries line numbers of its own,
which begin again at one, and the paragraph after a formula came out a
dozen blank lines down the page. A block with no source position ends the
run instead of starting a new count from a position that means nothing.

A packaged document carrying MathML now declares `properties=&amp;quot;mathml&amp;quot;`,
which is how a reading system decides whether it can render the document,
and without which the EPUB does not validate.

Documents the syntax in both READMEs and the manual, including when a `$`
is read as math and how to write a currency one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 &amp;lt;noreply@anthropic.com&amp;gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
    </content>
